2026-09-12. Primary-agent inspection and adversarial review. **DECISION REQUIRED;
no new symbolic family accepted or numeric allocation proposed.** Consumes the
[source direction receipt](LOCAL_RESERVE_PUBLIC_SOURCE_DIRECTION_ACCEPTANCE.md).

These bounds include one previously generated, completed delivery and the receiving
original. The number of generated local descendants is event count minus those two;
upstream delivery scheduling is excluded. They are not total MaxSettlementWork values.
Continuant/event counter increments are additional separate accounting, not runtime
slots. The positive envelopes use up to three detections and three role outputs;
the exact model cohort must establish which combinations and maxima are reachable.

Existing SEM241/242 layouts stay unchanged. Counter paths are keyed by ObserverId;
active membership paths use full212/213 perceptual file keys. Reuse the four already
declared attention perception accessors without renumbering, broadening their meaning
or replacing file keys with observer keys. The new tracking window has its own root
and accessor. All required canonical reads must agree with reconstructed tracking;
a private replay cache does not grant unlogged state access.

2026-09-12. **DECISION REQUIRED.** Memory content scarcity and nonreuse are settled;
the long-lived representation of source admission history is not. This blocks complete
public state/persistence shape, not the qualified selector or scheduler components.
